    "https://jobs.umw.edu/jobs/customer-service-representative-fredericksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Customer Service Representative",
      "description": "Customer Service Representative - Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States Applicant Login About UMW Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Aspire Org Chart Map Benefits Benefits for Faculty Medical / Health Insurance Leave Holidays Resources for Applicants FAQ Contact Us Search Jobs Using PUP Compensation Estimator Resources for Current Employees Hiring Compensation Using PUP Kiosk mode Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Customer Service Representative Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Full Time Closing on: Sep 8 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Customer Service Representative VP Area: Provost - UMW Department: Financial Aid Campus Location: Main Campus Advertised Range: $38,000 - $40,863 (A final salary offer will be determined by the selected candidate's qualifications, and is not is not negotiable beyond what is advertised.) Job Summary/Basic Functions The University of Mary Washington has an exciting opportunity to join our team as a Customer Service Representative. The Customer Service Representative serves as the first point of contact for students, families, prospective students, and campus partners seeking information regarding financial aid programs, processes, and policies. This highly visible, customer-facing position provides accurate, timely, and compassionate service through in-person, phone, email, and virtual interactions. The representative supports student success by assisting individuals in navigating federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid resources while ensuring compliance with applicable regulations and institutional policies. This position is not eligible for telework. Required KSAs/Competencies/Qualifications Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to build rapport with diverse populations of students and families. Strong problem-solving and conflict-resolution abilities. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Comfort using technology and learning new systems. Commitment to equity, inclusion, and student-centered service. Demonstrated commitment to providing outstanding customer service. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to explain complex information in a clear, student-friendly manner. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and database systems. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Required Experience: Previous experience in customer service, student services, financial services, higher education, or a related field. Required Education: N/A Required Licensure: N/A Additional Considerations: Associate degree in business, finance or accounting or related field or equivalent training and experience. Bachelor's degree from an accredited college/university in a related field. Experience in a college or university financial aid office. Knowledge of federal Title IV financial aid programs and regulations. Experience with student information systems and document management software. Bilingual or multilingual communication skills. Special Instructions You will be provided a confirmation of receipt when your application and/or résumé is submitted successfully. Please refer to “Your Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. To be considered for this position a state application must be received through the online employment system at https://jobs.umw.edu/ . Mailed, emailed, faxed, or hand-delivered applications or resumes will not be accepted. Excluding current UMW employees, selected candidate(s) must successfully pass a criminal history background check. Employment verification will be conducted to include current/previous supervisory employment reference checks. Other financial, credit, driving, background checks or completion of Statement of Economic Interests may be required for certain positions. For more information, please visit http://ethics.dls.virginia.gov/ . The University of Mary Washington adheres to the principle of equal opportunity. The University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, parental status (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliation, military service, or other non-merit based factors in recruiting, admitting, enrolling students or hiring and promoting faculty and staff members. Complaints of discrimination should be directed to the EEO officer of the University. UMW Values Veterans: UMW is a proud member of the Commonwealth of Virginia Values Veterans (V3) Program, authorized under the Code of Virginia (§2.2-2001.2). We are committed to recruiting, hiring, and retaining qualified Veterans and their spouses. Veterans who are hired into state positions may be eligible for additional leave accruals based on their total years of service in the military, National Guard or Reserve. For more information please visit: https://www.dhrm.virginia.gov/employeebenefits . In support of the Commonwealth’s commitment to inclusion, we are encouraging individuals with disabilities to apply through the Commonwealth Alternative Hiring Process (AHP). To be considered for this opportunity, applicants will need to provide their AHP Letter (formerly Certificate of Disability or COD) provided by the Department for Aging & Rehabilitative Services (DARS) or the Department for the Blind & Vision Impaired (DBVI). Service-Connected Veterans are encouraged to answer Veteran status questions and submit their disability documentation, if applicable, to DARS/DBVI to get their AHP Letter. Requesting an AHP Letter can be found at AHP Letter or by calling DARS at 800-552-5019. Note: Applicants who received a Certificate of Disability from DARS or DBVI dated between April 1, 2022- February 29, 2024, can still use that COD as applicable documentation for the Alternative Hiring Process. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) db79022c Last Name (required) 55d10643 Email (required) ea4bb7f0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Financial Aid Peer Counselor Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Admissions Responsibilities include receiving and answering basic financial aid-related questions for incoming customers via telephone, e-mail, and front desk reception; intelligently explaining to customers basic information about Federal Student Aid programs and processes; providing excellent customer service while maintaining confidentiality of students’ records appropriate to FERPA regulations; working closely with the Financial Aid Customer Service Team. Student Facility Assistant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Facilities Operations Help UMW Grounds keep campus beautiful! Collect recycling and trash from cans and toters around campus. Must be comfortable driving a university truck around campus. Must complete UMW Van Familiarization before starting. Senior Accountant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Finance This position supports the financial operations of the institution by independently performing complex accounting and reconciliation functions in accordance with institutional policies, state and federal regulations, and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). STARS Ambassador - Center for STARS Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Registrar's Office The Center for STARS is seeking hardworking, organized, and self-motivated students to serve as STARS Ambassadors. Ambassadors assist with office operations, help plan events, and represent STARS at campus and community programs. This role provides an opportunity to connect with prospective and current students, share your UMW experience, and serve as a positive representative of the university. Grounds Lead Worker Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Grounds Support the Landscape & Grounds mission of maintaining the UMW landscape & grounds in a safe, neat, clean and aesthetically pleasing manner. The UMW Landscape & Grounds Department strives to provide exceptional service and a safe environment to the UMW community and visitors, while being an environmental steward in maintaining a beautiful and inviting university. Contracts & Resourcing Manager Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Capital Outlay The University of Mary Washington has an exciting opportunity to join our team as a Contracts & Resourcing Manager. Hear about jobs that are right for you? Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c720e6bc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Financial Aid Financial Aid Categories Staff Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time First Name (required) 3cbc3dcd Last Name (required) 8c1f2a84 Email (required) d892e86e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Candidate Details Please choose the employment type(s)"
