    "https://jobs.umw.edu/jobs/women-s-lacrosse-assistant-coach-fredericksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Women's Lacrosse Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Women's Lacrosse Assistant Coach - Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States Applicant Login About UMW Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Aspire Org Chart Map Benefits Benefits for Faculty Medical / Health Insurance Leave Holidays Resources for Applicants FAQ Contact Us Search Jobs Using PUP Compensation Estimator Resources for Current Employees Hiring Compensation Using PUP Kiosk mode Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Women's Lacrosse Assistant Coach Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Part Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Women's Lacrosse Assistant Coach VP Area: President - UMW Department: Lacrosse-Women's Campus Location: Main Campus Advertised Range: $25,000 stipend (A final salary offer will be determined by the selected candidate's qualifications, and is not is not negotiable beyond what is advertised.) Job Summary/Basic Functions The University of Mary Washington, an NCAA Division III institution located in historic and vibrant Fredericksburg, VA, is seeking a part time assistant coach. Graduate tuition remission may be possible after one year of employment. Coaching Athletic Assistant duties include, but are not limited to, assisting the head coach with practice and game preparation and coaching, recruiting, academics, fundraising, and the off-season program. Required KSAs/Competencies/Qualifications Ability to recruit, coach and teach highly talented student-athletes. Proven record in following directives and being responsible for tasks which have been assigned. Ability to scout opponents and break down game tapes, develop scouting and highlight reels. Ability to adhere to all policies, rules and regulations of the university, the C2C and the NCAA. Ability to organize work effectively, conceptualize and prioritize objectives and exercise independent judgment based on an understanding of organizational policies and activities. Ability to integrate resources, policies, and information for the determination of procedures, solutions, and other outcomes. Ability to establish and maintain professional and effective work relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the public. Ability to communicate effectively orally, by phone, in person, and in writing with great attention to detail. Ability to respond to emergency situations in a timely manner. Ability to represent the department and University in a friendly, courteous and professional manner. Required Experience: 2-4 years experience as a Girls/Women's Lacrosse Coach. Experience coaching at the collegiate level. Experience as a student athlete in Lacrosse. Additional Considerations: KSAs: An expressed interest in collegiate coaching. EDUCATION: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college/university in a related field or equivalent training and experience. Experience: Experience playing on a Lacrosse team at the collegiate level. Special Instructions This position is open until filled. After 5 business days, this recruitment may be closed at any time. You will be provided a confirmation of receipt when your application and/or résumé is submitted successfully. Please refer to “Your Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. To be considered for this position a state application must be received through the online employment system at https://jobs.umw.edu/ . Mailed, emailed, faxed, or hand-delivered applications or resumes will not be accepted. Excluding current UMW employees, selected candidate(s) must successfully pass a criminal history background check. Employment verification will be conducted to include current/previous supervisory employment reference checks. Other financial, credit, driving, background checks or completion of Statement of Economic Interests may be required for certain positions. For more information, please visit http://ethics.dls.virginia.gov/ . The University of Mary Washington adheres to the principle of equal opportunity. The University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, parental status (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliation, military service, or other non-merit based factors in recruiting, admitting, enrolling students or hiring and promoting faculty and staff members. Complaints of discrimination should be directed to the EEO officer of the University. UMW Values Veterans: UMW is a proud member of the Commonwealth of Virginia Values Veterans (V3) Program, authorized under the Code of Virginia (§2.2-2001.2). We are committed to recruiting, hiring, and retaining qualified Veterans and their spouses. Veterans who are hired into state positions may be eligible for additional leave accruals based on their total years of service in the military, National Guard or Reserve. For more information please visit: https://www.dhrm.virginia.gov/employeebenefits . In support of the Commonwealth’s commitment to inclusion, we are encouraging individuals with disabilities to apply through the Commonwealth Alternative Hiring Process (AHP). To be considered for this opportunity, applicants will need to provide their AHP Letter (formerly Certificate of Disability or COD) provided by the Department for Aging & Rehabilitative Services (DARS) or the Department for the Blind & Vision Impaired (DBVI). Service-Connected Veterans are encouraged to answer Veteran status questions and submit their disability documentation, if applicable, to DARS/DBVI to get their AHP Letter. Requesting an AHP Letter can be found at AHP Letter or by calling DARS at 800-552-5019. Note: Applicants who received a Certificate of Disability from DARS or DBVI dated between April 1, 2022- February 29, 2024, can still use that COD as applicable documentation for the Alternative Hiring Process. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2d0e5873 Last Name (required) 915e375a Email (required) fbdc364d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Financial Aid Peer Counselor Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Admissions Responsibilities include receiving and answering basic financial aid-related questions for incoming customers via telephone, e-mail, and front desk reception; intelligently explaining to customers basic information about Federal Student Aid programs and processes; providing excellent customer service while maintaining confidentiality of students’ records appropriate to FERPA regulations; working closely with the Financial Aid Customer Service Team. Student Facility Assistant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Facilities Operations Help UMW Grounds keep campus beautiful! Collect recycling and trash from cans and toters around campus. Must be comfortable driving a university truck around campus. Must complete UMW Van Familiarization before starting. Senior Accountant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Finance This position supports the financial operations of the institution by independently performing complex accounting and reconciliation functions in accordance with institutional policies, state and federal regulations, and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). STARS Ambassador - Center for STARS Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Registrar's Office The Center for STARS is seeking hardworking, organized, and self-motivated students to serve as STARS Ambassadors. Ambassadors assist with office operations, help plan events, and represent STARS at campus and community programs. This role provides an opportunity to connect with prospective and current students, share your UMW experience, and serve as a positive representative of the university. Customer Service Representative Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Financial Aid The Customer Service Representative serves as the first point of contact for students, families, prospective students, and campus partners seeking information regarding financial aid programs, processes, and policies. Grounds Lead Worker Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Grounds Support the Landscape & Grounds mission of maintaining the UMW landscape & grounds in a safe, neat, clean and aesthetically pleasing manner. The UMW Landscape & Grounds Department strives to provide exceptional service and a safe environment to the UMW community and visitors, while being an environmental steward in maintaining a beautiful and inviting university. Hear about jobs that are right for you? Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e916fb0b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Lacrosse-Women's Lacrosse-Women's Categories Staff Staff Employment Type Part Time Part Time First Name (required) 2db90d25 Last Name (required) f551e5b2 Email (required) 91e181f3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Candidate Details Please choose the employment type(s)"
