    "https://jobs.umw.edu/jobs/intern-career-workforce-programs-rwalc-fredericksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Intern, Career & Workforce Programs",
      "description": "Intern, Career & Workforce Programs - RWALC - Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States Applicant Login About UMW Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Aspire Org Chart Map Benefits Benefits for Faculty Medical / Health Insurance Leave Holidays Resources for Applicants FAQ Contact Us Search Jobs Using PUP Compensation Estimator Resources for Current Employees Hiring Compensation Using PUP Kiosk mode Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Intern, Career & Workforce Programs - RWALC Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Student Employee Add to favorites View favorites Title: Intern, Career & Workforce Programs - RWALC VP Area: Provost - UMW Department: Center for Career and Professional Development Campus Location: Main Campus Advertised Range: $15 per hour Job Summary/Basic Functions • Draft and edit templates and content for emails, newsletters, websites, and social media related to programs and events • Assist with promotion, planning, and on site/virtual support for events such as workshops, information sessions, regional events, and employer and student programs • Assist with event preparation, including setup, breakdown, material organization, and follow-up communication • Update web pages and digital resources under staff guidance to ensure timely, accurate information • Maintain contact lists, communication trackers, and basic event and program data • Provide support for data-related tasks, including organizing spreadsheets and gaining exposure to basic data analysis • Provide general administrative and project support including special projects as assigned by staff • Maintain confidentiality and follow campus and office policies Required KSAs/Competencies/Qualifications • Currently enrolled in an undergraduate program • Interest in workforce and/or economic development, human resources, communications, or higher education • Intermediate computer skills including Microsoft 365 and AI with a willingness to learn new software and tools • Strong organizational skills and attention to detail • Reliable, responsible, punctual, and professional demeanor • Ability to follow instructions and work independently or as part of a team Required Experience: None Required Education: Undergraduate coursework and current UMW student Required Licensure: None Additional Considerations: Preferred Skills (Not Required) • Familiarity with web design tools or platforms (e.g., basic HTML, WordPress, Canva) • Experience or interest in content creation (writing, graphics, or multimedia) • Basic knowledge of spreadsheets or data visualization tools • Strong written and verbal communication skills • Customer service experience or interest Special Instructions You will be provided a confirmation of receipt when your application and/or résumé is submitted successfully. Please refer to “Your Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. To be considered for this position a state application must be received through the online employment system at https://jobs.umw.edu/ . Mailed, emailed, faxed, or hand-delivered applications or resumes will not be accepted. Excluding current UMW employees, selected candidate(s) must successfully pass a criminal history background check. Employment verification will be conducted to include current/previous supervisory employment reference checks. Other financial, credit, driving, background checks or completion of Statement of Economic Interests may be required for certain positions. For more information, please visit http://ethics.dls.virginia.gov/ . The University of Mary Washington adheres to the principle of equal opportunity. The University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, parental status (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliation, military service, or other non-merit based factors in recruiting, admitting, enrolling students or hiring and promoting faculty and staff members. Complaints of discrimination should be directed to the EEO officer of the University. UMW Values Veterans: UMW is a proud member of the Commonwealth of Virginia Values Veterans (V3) Program, authorized under the Code of Virginia (§2.2-2001.2). We are committed to recruiting, hiring, and retaining qualified Veterans and their spouses. Veterans who are hired into state positions may be eligible for additional leave accruals based on their total years of service in the military, National Guard or Reserve. For more information please visit: https://www.dhrm.virginia.gov/employeebenefits . In support of the Commonwealth’s commitment to inclusion, we are encouraging individuals with disabilities to apply through the Commonwealth Alternative Hiring Process (AHP). To be considered for this opportunity, applicants will need to provide their AHP Letter (formerly Certificate of Disability or COD) provided by the Department for Aging & Rehabilitative Services (DARS) or the Department for the Blind & Vision Impaired (DBVI). Service-Connected Veterans are encouraged to answer Veteran status questions and submit their disability documentation, if applicable, to DARS/DBVI to get their AHP Letter. Requesting an AHP Letter can be found at AHP Letter or by calling DARS at 800-552-5019. Note: Applicants who received a Certificate of Disability from DARS or DBVI dated between April 1, 2022- February 29, 2024, can still use that COD as applicable documentation for the Alternative Hiring Process. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 110f1fe5 Last Name (required) bb4c89d6 Email (required) 7abaad58 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Financial Aid Peer Counselor Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Admissions Responsibilities include receiving and answering basic financial aid-related questions for incoming customers via telephone, e-mail, and front desk reception; intelligently explaining to customers basic information about Federal Student Aid programs and processes; providing excellent customer service while maintaining confidentiality of students’ records appropriate to FERPA regulations; working closely with the Financial Aid Customer Service Team. Student Facility Assistant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Facilities Operations Help UMW Grounds keep campus beautiful! Collect recycling and trash from cans and toters around campus. Must be comfortable driving a university truck around campus. Must complete UMW Van Familiarization before starting. Senior Accountant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Finance This position supports the financial operations of the institution by independently performing complex accounting and reconciliation functions in accordance with institutional policies, state and federal regulations, and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). STARS Ambassador - Center for STARS Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Registrar's Office The Center for STARS is seeking hardworking, organized, and self-motivated students to serve as STARS Ambassadors. Ambassadors assist with office operations, help plan events, and represent STARS at campus and community programs. This role provides an opportunity to connect with prospective and current students, share your UMW experience, and serve as a positive representative of the university. Customer Service Representative Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Financial Aid The Customer Service Representative serves as the first point of contact for students, families, prospective students, and campus partners seeking information regarding financial aid programs, processes, and policies. Grounds Lead Worker Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Grounds Support the Landscape & Grounds mission of maintaining the UMW landscape & grounds in a safe, neat, clean and aestheti