      "description": "Senior Carpenter - Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States Applicant Login About UMW Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Aspire Org Chart Map Benefits Benefits for Faculty Medical / Health Insurance Leave Holidays Resources for Applicants FAQ Contact Us Search Jobs Using PUP Compensation Estimator Resources for Current Employees Hiring Compensation Using PUP Kiosk mode Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Carpenter Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Senior Carpenter VP Area: Administration & Finance - UMW Department: Carpenter Shop Campus Location: Main Campus Advertised Range: $45,176 - $48,338 Job Summary/Basic Functions The University of Mary Washington has an exciting opportunity to join our team as a Senior Carpenter. The Senior Carpenter performs highly skilled carpentry work in one or more of the following modes: serves as project leader; serves as team leader and/or team member; works independently to provide senior-level carpentry tasks. Required KSAs/Competencies/Qualifications Considerable knowledge of all phases of carpentry and building maintenance Working knowledge of math, including fractions and decimals Considerable skills in the use of hand and power tools related to the carpentry trade Demonstrated ability to follow written and oral instructions Required Experience: Considerable experience in the carpentry trade Considerable experience with maintaining records Considerable experience interpreting drawings, blueprints, and work orders Considerable experience making cost estimates of labor and materials Considerable experience working in confined spaces and working from heights, ladders and scaffolding Considerable experience performing manual labor, including lifting and carrying equipment and tools to and from job sites Additional Considerations: EDUCATION: High school graduate or equivalent Vocational or trade school training in carpentry Special Instructions This position is open until filled. Priority first review of applications will be conducted on applications submitted by January 30, 2026 . Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. To be considered for this position a state application must be received through the online employment system at https://jobs.umw.edu/. Selected candidate(s) must successfully pass a criminal history background check. Employment verification will be conducted to include current/previous supervisory employment reference checks. Other financial, credit, driving, background checks or completion of Statement of Economic Interests may be required for certain positions. For more information, please visit http://ethics.dls.virginia.gov/. The University of Mary Washington adheres to the principle of equal opportunity. The University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, parental status (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliation, military service, or other non-merit based factors in recruiting, admitting, enrolling students or hiring and promoting faculty and staff members. Complaints of discrimination should be directed to the AA/EEO officer of the University. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 0636e5db Last Name (required) cf3a4a0d Email (required) 528d2956 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Financial Aid Peer Counselor Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Admissions Responsibilities include receiving and answering basic financial aid-related questions for incoming customers via telephone, e-mail, and front desk reception; intelligently explaining to customers basic information about 